owing statements are true?\n\nI. ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nII. ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n\nIII. ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$"] ["question-17a8497e-763c-5804-a8ea-e63d106be3fe" :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true while statement II is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/1d/1d91a85ccbb948e070db738373ffc5032f4e91a0ba8e04cd14e79276b0e798f8.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/a8/a8e0bffd04fb7b765d3c654f62b1958ab55a42f0d26cbc9f2b2e31f7d8e6f775.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""] ["question-17a8497e-763c-5804-a8ea-e63d106be3fe" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-be155506-4e79-5a1a-866f-997f1cb30ccc" :answer-field/id #uuid "be155506-4e79-5a1a-866f-997f1cb30ccc"] ["answer-d9563607-dd70-5767-87cb-3d112f17eed5" :answer/id #uuid "d9563607-dd70-5767-87cb-3d112f17eed5"] ["answer-d9563607-dd70-5767-87cb-3d112f17eed5" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-d9563607-dd70-5767-87cb-3d112f17eed5" :answer/value "I and III only"] ["answer-0ac92f55-bdd5-5ebb-8623-7211f79f9620" :answer/id #uuid "0ac92f55-bdd5-5ebb-8623-7211f79f9620"] ["answer-0ac92f55-bdd5-5ebb-8623-7211f79f9620" :answer/type :a